  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) achieves 0.653 accuracy, while the only image-only test (resnet50, singleprofile) yields a very low 0.208 accuracy. This single data point is insufficient to determine whether the image modality carries any useful signal or whether resnet50 is simply a poor encoder for this task. Question: Does a stronger, ImageNet-pretrained encoder (ViT-L) reveal any meaningful image signal? This is a single-variable change (encoder only) from config_010, isolating the effect of representation quality. Why this is the best next experiment: Before committing limited budget to any of the 36 multimodal configurations, we must establish whether image features are informative at all. If ViT-L also performs near-chance, we can confidently abandon multimodal fusion and focus remaining experiments on refining the RNA-only pipeline (e.g., scvi_n200 singleprofile, scgpt+transformer). If ViT-L substantially improves over resnet50, it justifies investing in multimodal fusion with the stronger encoder. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design decision (include image or not) with minimal confounding."
